{"body":"## Summary\nWP-1312 of v1.1.4 (3/3, stacked on #445 which is stacked on #442; retarget as each merges).\n\n- `nexus worktree merge [target] [--no-squash] [--no-rebase] [--no-remove] [-m msg]`, run from inside the worktree: commit dirty changes (deterministic message from the existing `generateConventionalCommit`, or `-m`), back up to `refs/nexus-backup/<branch>` (a commit of the working tree exactly as `add -A` sees it, built with a temporary index; untouched branch), squash, rebase onto the target, fast-forward only in the target's worktree, then remove the worktree and branch. A rebase conflict leaves the rebase open in the worktree with files listed and the target untouched. Refuses: main checkout, detached HEAD, dirty target worktree, rebase/merge already in progress, target not checked out, diverged `--no-rebase`.\n- `nexus worktree prune [--dry-run] [--min-age 1d] [--limit N] [--discard-ignored]`: removes worktrees whose HEAD is integrated into the default branch (same commit, ancestor, empty three-dot diff, same tree, patch-id), clean, and last touched (dir mtime or HEAD commit time) longer ago than `--min-age`. Never the main checkout, the current worktree, locked worktrees or `nexus/<task>` speculative worktrees; ignored-file holders kept unless `--discard-ignored`; bounded by `--limit` (default 100) because this host has 874 worktrees; stale (missing-directory) registrations are cleared with `git worktree prune`.\n- All Git calls via the pinned helper: hooks (pre-commit, commit-msg, post-commit, post-merge, pre-rebase, post-rewrite, reference-transaction) verified not to run.\n- Read-only: `merge` refused; `prune` only with `--dry-run`, in the command layer and both slash gates.\n- A marked `preMerge` seam in `merge.ts` is where WP-1313's blocking hook attaches; `removeOne` is exported for it.\n- Includes the PLAN section 5 acceptance flow as one test.\n\nNot in this PR (stated plainly): the validation-receipt gate (CAND-001..004) for named-worktree merges. That gate is built from an in-memory receipt produced by an agent run (`WorktreeManager.mergeWorktree`, unchanged); a standalone CLI merge has no receipt, and running a project verifier from it is exactly the approval-gated execution WP-1313 defines. LLM-generated commit messages (the plan says optional) are not implemented; no external command is ever run.\n\n## Tests\nRed first: the test-only commit fails 9/9 (unknown subcommand `merge`/`prune`). Green at head: `CI=true node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/worktrunk_merge.test.ts` pass 9 / fail 0; `test/worktrunk_core.test.ts test/worktrunk_copy.test.ts` pass 20 / fail 0; `test/slash_router.test.ts test/repl_readonly_commands.test.ts` pass 36 / fail 0. `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ (http://localhost:9200) reachable (opencode index flagged unverified). Consulted: `xerj code opencode \"worktree remove prune stale merge fast-forward rebase\" -k 3 --full 300`; `xerj search --prefix codex|kilocode|goose \"git wo…2062 tokens truncated…n- worktrunk_merge 26/0, worktrunk_core 12/0, worktrunk_review 29/0, worktrunk_copy 15/0, repl_readonly_commands 1/0, config 17/0, slash_router 35/1 (`!`, daemon), `tsc` clean.\n\n### Entire round 4b (head `997e0193`; `origin/main` d6a8ad92 and #442 `328c559e` merged; the Worktrunk ledger is now section G because main added its own F)\n- `01M710PQYNB4` (medium) FIXED: `clearStaleEntry` re-reads the entry under the lock and leaves a recreated, changed or locked one alone. Red: \"prune does not force-remove a stale entry that was recreated while it waited for the lock\". worktrunk_merge 27/0.\n\n### Entire round 5 (head `b050d581`; `origin/main` d6a8ad92 and #442 `0ebd3928` merged)\n- `01M70YN4DJN5` (medium) now FIXED (the earlier BLOCKED note is obsolete: the claim on `workspace_commands.ts` was released): the slash handler calls `relocationAfter` and `host.setWorkspace`; slash_router asserts the session moves and the durable paths stay valid.\n- `01M710R4BMPZ` (medium) FIXED: `Agent.setWorkspace` rebinds the primary workspace identity to an explicitly selected live directory when the directory the session started in is gone or replaced (before, only re-selecting the same path did). Red: \"an agent that started inside a worktree can be moved out of it after the worktree is merged away, with its durable state still valid\". state 18/0, persistence_protection 27/0, recover_worktree_conversation 3/0, approval_policy 15/0; verifier_gating (4 fail), experimental_and_readonly (1 fail) and objective_continuation (10 fail) fail identically at the pre-change snapshot (environment).\n- worktrunk_merge 27/0, worktrunk_core 12/0, worktrunk_review 29/0, worktrunk_copy 15/0, repl_readonly_commands 1/0, config 17/0, slash_router 36/1 (`!`, daemon), `tsc` clean.\n\n### Entire round 6 (head `ad2aa1ec`)\n- `01M7117BZ4HW` (medium) FIXED: `tokenizeWorktreeArgs` honours single and double quotes (shell-style, no escapes), so `/worktree merge ^ -m \"feat: add login\"` keeps its message. Red: \"a quoted merge message survives the interactive tokenizer and becomes the commit message\". worktrunk_merge 28/0; worktrunk_core 12/0, worktrunk_review 29/0, worktrunk_copy 15/0, repl_readonly_commands 1/0, config 17/0, slash_router 36/1 (`!`, daemon), `tsc` clean.\n\n## Could not verify\n- Behaviour against `wt` 0.81.0 was not compared (not run).\n- Signed-commit setups (`commit.gpgsign=true` would need an agent/pinentry; stdin is closed, so the command fails with Git's message).\n- Full `make test` and Git 2.54/macOS/Windows.\n- `test/sidecar.test.ts` approvals/cancellation tests are timing-sensitive on this loaded host (one run failed `cancel during inference ... promptly`, isolated re-runs pass 7/7); the worktree changes only touch the `/worktree` gate lines there.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","closedAt":"2026-11-11T08:22:44Z","headRefOid":"a60e8edc2e57bf74e7a51b7ba38d5d120beff91d","mergeCommit":nul