docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:144:| RD-6 | Session fork (reference: Cline `core/src/session/fork-metadata.ts`) | fork test: two divergent continuations, both resumable | M | P2 | Note 2026-11-18: PARTIAL. Done: `SessionManager.forkSession(sourceId, {atMessage?, newId?})` (`cli/src/session.ts`) and `/fork [message-count]` in the TUI catalogue and the REPL. The source is only read (tests compare its record, message log and archive byte for byte after a fork and after the fork continues). The cut backs up to the last complete tool exchange. Compactions whose summary is still in the kept conversation keep their record and archive lines (copied verbatim, so `auditCompactionsOnResume` verifies the fork); a compaction whose summary the cut removed is left out of the fork (otherwise resume would undo it into history the operator did not choose). The fork records `forkedFrom`. Test: two divergent continuations, both resumable and both auditing clean. Decisions: the objective ledger is carried only by a fork of the whole conversation (a truncated fork never reached the source's later state); worktree binding, in-flight operation, provider recovery and last turn are not carried. Update 2026-11-18: the start flag is done: `nexus run --fork-session <task> [--fork-at <n>]` (task store, as `--resume`), `nexus repl --fork-session <id>` and `nexus --fork-session <id>` (opens the REPL, not the TUI: the TUI binary is not given a session to open). Flag errors (unknown source, bad `--fork-at`, `--fork-session` with `--resume`) exit 2. Forking a session bound to a worktree is REFUSED, by design: the binding names one checkout and a fork would share it (either session's merge or discard would pull it from under the other); `/fork` refuses while a worktree is active. Not done: carrying a worktree binding (needs a decision on creating a second checkout), keeping `forkedFrom` after the fork's own turns are saved, and an automated test of the REPL `/fork` worktree refusal (the TUI slash path is tested)